ild_lib answers 'unchanged' when a repo's tracked generated src already matches the store, so rebuild_lib skips the crate build and a fresh install never produces an artifact - dev.github.import/update now build the crate unconditionally.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,flowlang,builder,ffi,bug\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295573656\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Store meta.json cargo dependencies are the source the builder regenerates crate Cargo.tomls from - bumping a crate version in a Cargo.toml without updating the owning library's store meta makes every subsequent rebuild silently regress it. The 2026-08-09 flowlang 0.3.31 / ndata 0.3.17 sync had this latent regression via data/app/meta.json (still 0.3.30/0.3.16, masked by Cargo.lock semver compatibility); fixed via save_library_config on the nebula-overhaul branch. Corollary: dev.dev.compile on a newbound_core-rooted library builds only the newbound_core package as an error check - the host binary relink is a separate explicit `cargo build` at the checkout root, per the interim-process restart table.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,build,meta.json,cargo,drift\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295580721\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_groups derives the ENFORCED readers arrays from the groups string at save time, at all three levels: library meta.json; control record plus its inline data records (app.read's gate); command META record (the array check_security reads via lookup_command_id) plus impl record. Empty groups derives [] = admin-only. Returns changed/groups/readers.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Restores the retired editcontrol/editcommand derivation (readers = groups.split(',')). Library-level readers refresh into system.libraries on restart. writers is never t