rrent.\",\n    \"tags\": \"flowlang,drift,stale\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"the owner's correction of a reverted mistake, in session, 2026-08-05\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785944284307\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Every LLM provider behind agent.llm's resolver accepts exactly ONE system message, and it must be at index 0.\",\n    \"detail\": \"vLLM's chat template answers a system message at any later index — including index 1, ahead of every user turn — with a hard 400: BadRequestError \\\"System message must be at the beginning.\\\" So client-side context injection (recall layer 4's mode pack) must be APPENDED to the existing system message, never inserted beside it. Appending rather than prepending is also the cache-friendly choice: the curriculum stays a stable prefix, so server-side prefix caching still hits. agent.agentloop's chatTurn does this in convo(), which builds a merged COPY — the venue's own messages array is never mutated.\",\n    \"tags\": \"llm,agent,platform-api,wire\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"lib\": \"agent\",\n      \"ctl\": \"agentloop\",\n      \"facet\": \"js\",\n      \"hash\": \"6569fbeed2ace744\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1785964641067\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.github.import is the drop-in library install path: given a git URL whose repo has data/<lib> and runtime/<lib> at its root, it clones into repositories/<lib>, symlinks both into the instance, calls load_library then rebuild_lib. dev.github has only import and list — no update or remove; update today is `git pull` in repositories/<lib> plus rebuild_lib by hand. A brand-new FFI root additionally needs `newbound rebuild` + host build + restart before the watcher and initializer know the crate.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,dev.github,install,ffi\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/dev/github/import.rs, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786