nd record therefore means admin-only — the right default for commands that shell out to sudo.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,security,readers,groups\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"newbound_core/src/security/security/init.rs check_security, verified 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786292476517\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The flowlang builder has three verified gaps around FFI library crates (all worked around, all wanting an upstream flow-repo PR): (1) the default generated Cargo.toml declares serde/serde_json optional deps but omits the serde_support/python_runtime/javascript_runtime feature blocks, so any compile passing --features=serde_support fails until the features are added - which is why the agent/kb/scratch/nebula repos track their crate Cargo.tomls by hand; (2) the generated <ctl>/mod.rs cmdinit is append-only across regenerations - stale command ids accumulate (a delete+re-upsert leaves both generations registered) and the built dylib lags the sources by one compile - the clean reset is delete the generated src dir and run `newbound rebuild`; (3) build_lib answers 'unchanged' when a repo's tracked generated src already matches the store, so rebuild_lib skips the crate build and a fresh install never produces an artifact - dev.github.import/update now build the crate unconditionally.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,flowlang,builder,ffi,bug\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295573656\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"Store meta.json cargo dependencies are the source the builder regenerates crate Cargo.tomls from - bumping a crate version in a Cargo.toml without updating the owning library's store meta makes every subsequent rebuild silently regress it. The 2026-08-09 flowlang 0.3.31 / ndata 0.3.17 sync had this latent regression via data/app/meta.json (still 0.3.30/0.3.16, masked by Cargo.lock sem