ewbound_core-rooted library builds only the newbound_core package as an error check - the host binary relink is a separate explicit `cargo build` at the checkout root, per the interim-process restart table.\",\n    \"tags\": \"platform-api,build,meta.json,cargo,drift\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"verified live during the nebula overhaul, 2026-08-09\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786295580721\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"dev.code.set_groups derives the ENFORCED readers arrays from the groups string at save time, at all three levels: library meta.json; control record plus its inline data records (app.read's gate); command META record (the array check_security reads via lookup_command_id) plus impl record. Empty groups derives [] = admin-only. Returns changed/groups/readers.\",\n    \"detail\": \"Restores the retired editcontrol/editcommand derivation (readers = groups.split(',')). Library-level readers refresh into system.libraries on restart. writers is never touched (only app.delete consults it).\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,set_groups,readers,dev.code\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390464\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"patch_command_body, set_command_imports, and upsert_command preserve existing readers/writers on the records they rewrite; before 2026-08-09 every code edit reset a gated command to admin-only, because flowlang's data::write::write stamps whatever arrays it is passed.\",\n    \"tags\": \"security,readers,dev.code,preservation\",\n    \"source\": {\n      \"doc\": \"authored+verified on a disposable, session 2026-08-09 (branch claude/dev-ui-security-integration-lnonp5)\"\n    },\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786309390468\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"check_security's group loop passes when the library readers contain 'anonymous'