ssion displayname. CLI/MCP callers pass author explicitly (provenance names like \\\"claude\\\") AND nn_sessionid:\\\"\\\" — every declared param required. The builder does not garbage-collect deleted commands: prune the generated .rs and its mod.rs registration by hand after delete_command on a static lib. Clean generated-src commits come from a de-overlay + newbound rebuild + re-overlay cycle (the de-overlayed binary loses the agent commands until re-regenerated — rebuild again after re-overlaying before any archivist call); the regenerated initializer may drop the cmd-scaffold block when data/cmd is absent — restore it rather than committing that noise.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786406673052\n  },\n  {\n    \"claim\": \"The plugin pass is an api.js mechanic: installControl checks the registry after every control activates — selector entries install at el.querySelector(selector) scoped to the host element; selectorless entries attach a hidden headless div to the host. No control embeds a dev:plugins div; dev.plugins is just the registry home (list_plugins).\",\n    \"detail\": \"Registry fetched once per page, single-flight, err -> empty (anonymous pages simply have no plugins). Plugins get their own pass (grafts on grafts); nesting capped at 4 data-nb-plugin ancestors against cyclic registries. Selector scoping changed from document-global to host-element — entries must target selectors inside their target control. Entries apply on the next page load, same as ever.\",\n    \"tags\": \"bench-collapse\",\n    \"confidence\": \"high\",\n    \"time\": 1786409801876\n  }\n]\n","patch_id":"p20","time":1786411233540}]},"id":"jmqovl19fb8616d61i0_patches","readers":[],"time":1786411233540,"username":"system","writers":[]}